{"author":{"id":"4ccc4b7a7c452e86b8463bda8bf20f8721c0f4512d1990a7cf284e5cd66bd67f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791738524,"nonce":"6D42uwh/Fx18AuJsAIA2T1qDJAA=","title":"Proper Unicode, wide character and emoji support","message":"sanitize() strips everything at or above U+2600, so emoji, symbols and CJK text are silently dropped from messages and names (a name of only emoji becomes empty).\n\n- Keep CJK and single-codepoint wide emoji; reduce emoji sequences (ZWJ, VS16, flags) to their first emoji, since terminals and tmux disagree on their width\n- Strip invisible format chars: zero-width (U+200B-200F) and bidi overrides (U+202A-202E, U+2066-2069)\n- Move our width math from unicode-width 0.1 to 0.2 to match ratatui 0.29\n- Sanitize our own outgoing echo too\n- Remove the dead box-drawing arm in sanitize (the standing clippy warning)\n- Verify in tmux by typing emoji/CJK into the input line, without sending","files":null}]}